Title: Oxfordshire child's 'harrowing' struggle to fit in at school
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': 'Lauren, not her real name, said her child\'s anxiety around school became so severe they once told her they "didn\'t want to live any more".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 114}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': 'She said her child found it "very difficult to do anything normal... most of the time they spend half an hour in school each day".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 115}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': 'Sometimes Lauren would wait with her child at school for up to two hours.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 70}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': '"You can tell they can\'t cope with being there," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 49}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': '"Am I imagining these things? Am I a bad parent? You question all those things when, deep down, you know your child and you know they\'re unhappy".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': '"The frustration of them not having those opportunities to fit into a normal education system is really harrowing."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 102}}, {'Speaker': 'Heather Richards', 'Text': 'Head teacher Heather Richards said missing school could become a "vicious circle" but that the sessions had led to "real improvement" in attendance figures.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 153}}, {'Speaker': 'Heather Richards', 'Text': '"They have a stronger connection with some of the children in their year group," she added. "They also build their confidence."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': 'Lauren\'s child attends an online version of the sessions and said they "literally leap" to go to attend.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Speaker': 'Lauren', 'Text': '"Even if they\'re having a really bad week, they\'ll go to that session and they\'ll come out really buoyant and happy," she said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 109}}, {'Speaker': 'Department for Education', 'Text': 'In a statement, the Department for Education said; "The government inherited a broken system, with children and families facing poor outcomes and barriers to opportunity.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 141}}, {'Speaker': 'Department for Education', 'Text': '"The case for tackling the epidemic of school absence could not be clearer: improved grades, higher wages, better life chances.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Speaker': 'Department for Education', 'Text': '"Tackling this issue is everyone\'s responsibility – government, schools, parents, and children – and we need a national effort to get our kids back in the classroom.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 131}}, {'Speaker': 'Department for Education', 'Text': '"As part of our plan for change, we are determined to turn the tide on poor attendance and break down barriers to opportunity - whether it\'s through attendance mentors, free breakfast clubs, improved mental health support, additional investment in family support, or more focus from Ofsted."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 218}}], 'Description': [], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Four schoolchildren sit in a school playground with their backs to the camera. One child has been made to look partially transparent, with a white line outlining their silhouette.'}]}
